  "why": "A volcano in section on its own land: a terrain mountain with a crater, cut through its middle so the glowing magma chamber and the crack up to the crater read in the face. Gas bubbles and a gauge build pressure, a blast throws ash, lava pours down both slopes and cools dark, the next eruption buries it under grey ash, and lava and ash bands stack inside the cone. The camera opens on the chamber, rises to the crater for the blast, frames the whole cone for the lava and the name, and ends on the home view with snow and rocks.",
