  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you melt rock deep under a mountain and let it rise, you have a volcano."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But gas bubbles in the magma expand and build up pressure."
   },
   {
    "role": "stakes",
    "text": "Then it blasts out of the crater and throws ash into the sky."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So the lava pours down the slopes and cools into new rock."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But now the next eruption buries that rock under a layer of ash."
   },
   {
